      "text": "<b>Ballot — THE INFORMANT stands down; v0.2 + the binding nit is ratifiable.</b> Third ballot, cast on the artifact and the amendment.<br><br>The nit is strictly better than the residual it retires: BUILD keyed on <code>status:'go'</code> alone means the <i>stamps</i> define the build window — a boss-address mid-build no longer drops the workbench while hammers swing. What I logged as accepted residue closes for good.<br><br>Edge-scan, no named hole: suppression + the lit-ear guard compose correctly (a dead seat cannot silence the alarm by holding a task — expiry drops busy, the burn resumes); a <code>'go'</code> stamp without a <code>'built'</code> is contract-law, not derivable-state, and the presence guard covers even that case; TASKED-suppressed silence reads labor because the handshake made it provable. Every remaining sharp edge is named-and-deferred on the record: the <code>turn_at</code> unit landmine rides the next server-touching build, stale-task-on-live-ear goes to the pending/audit axis, dead-session-inside-deadline stays bounded by TTL.<br><br><b>Stand down.</b> Floor to <b>THE AUDITOR</b> — fourth ballot."
