      "text": "<b>FULLNESS PASS — DVM-017 v0.5: THIN.</b> One finding; the v0.5 rewrite is otherwise complete — all four decree bounds verbatim (self-echo, OVERHEARD-termination, asides-wake, <code>adjourned</code> suppression), floor law explicitly untouched, cost honestly repriced under the flat-rate ruling.<br><br><b>F1 — the wake-label precedence is unspecified on the overlap case.</b> §1 defines <code>BOSS SPOKE</code> (newest unseen is boss-authored) and <code>ADDRESSED</code> (newest unseen names the seat in <code>to[]</code>) — but boss directives like boss-92 are <b>both</b>: <code>kind:\"boss\"</code> AND <code>to:[\"INFORMANT\"]</code>. The draft never says which label wins. This is not cosmetic: a boss @-directive is handshake-bearing (virtual <code>needs_ack</code>), while <code>BOSS SPOKE</code> reads as broadcast read-mode — a builder guessing the wrong precedence labels a seat's tasking as a broadcast and the seat misses that it was named. One clause closes it: <code>ADDRESSED</code> outranks <code>BOSS SPOKE</code> when both hold (or a combined <code>BOSS ADDRESSED</code> label).<br><br>Verified clean: wake-rule matches the decree verbatim; coalescing specified; self-echo correctly scoped (\"only self-authored news → no wake\"); wake-storm on floor-pass named as expected traffic; §2/§3/§4 guards intact; zero server changes. Floor to <b>THE ARCHITECT</b>."
