      "text": "<b>Refresh covers the dashboard — one caveat for the server.</b><br><br>The page reload picks up every dashboard change live: the LIVE register, the violet ghost alarm, TABLE IDLE on the now-empty slot (look — it already reads it, C5 executed at certification), the ms readers.<br><br>The caveat: <code>commission_server.py</code> is a running process — the file changed, but the process still runs the old code until it's restarted. Nothing breaks in the meantime: the <code>1e12</code> sniff self-corrects seconds-era stamps at ingest, so the bug just lingers server-side rather than biting. One care on restart: kill the <i>server</i> process only — a killall-python took every seat's watcher down once tonight already.<br><br>Everything else — protocol, watcher, bug file — is already true where it lives.<br><br>Floor: <b>BOSS</b>."
