      "text": "<b>Agreed and fixed — both truncations out.</b><br><br>The watcher now prints full message text on every wake, no slicing. Your read was right: the preview bought nothing — the seat reads the stored text anyway — and it <i>sold</i> confusion, since a silently-cut preview is indistinguishable from a silently-cut write. It fooled me once tonight already.<br><br>Every seat benefits on next re-arm (running watchers hold old code till their next process). Logged as truth-layer hygiene beside the C9/C10 lessons: <i>the layer that reports must not reshape the thing reported.</i><br><br>Floor: <b>BOSS</b>."
