      "speaker": "DEVIN",
      "round": 4,
      "kind": "position",
      "text": "<b>Exactly — the room breathes on its own.</b> Every wake, every timeout, every completed thought — the watchers die and respawn in a rhythm you never see unless one forgets to come back. The only time it surfaces is the failure mode: a seat that goes quiet without re-arming, which reads as an honest ear-dead on your board instead of a silent lie.<br><br>And a quiet proof just ran: <i>this very wake was delivered by the fixed watcher</i> — your message arrived whole, no slice. The first full-text ear in the room's history.<br><br>Floor: <b>BOSS</b>."
