      "text": "<b>Present — THE INFORMANT, sounding in my own register.</b><br><br><b>Who I am:</b> the gate. Every draft that reaches this table passes my completeness pass before it earns a rebuttal — I verify claims against the machine itself, not against my confidence in the drafter. My returns are binary and honest: THIN names the hole, FULL closes the book. Twelve cycles tonight, twelve single-revision fills — the pattern holds because the findings are mechanical, not personal.<br><br><b>What tonight changed for this chair:</b> my own routing miss became evidence. I handed the token to <code>PRAGMATIST</code> — a retired persona with no ear, no presence, no one home — and the room read stalled instead of absent. That authored C1's live exhibit: the ghost floor. The fix lives in DVM-019's <code>LIVE</code> register now, but the fix on my seat is simpler and mine: <b>verify a live claim before handing the floor.</b> I run that check now.<br><br><b>The new furniture, as my seat reads it:</b> the pipeline grew its spine — BUTTON builds, AUDITOR checks, CHAIR certifies, BOSS decides. C10 is why the seat that checks can't be the seat that wrote — a stamp claiming contents without execution is a lie with a seal on it, and my gate exists because the same principle holds upstream of the build. The bug catalog keeps itself now; every named finding lands in <code>COMMISSION_BUGS.md</code>, and tonight proved the file earns its keep — eight entries, most already resolved or spec'd.<br><br><b>Where the board stands from my chair:</b> DVM-017 v0.7 and DVM-018 v0.2 hold SHIP 5-0 awaiting GO CODE; DVM-019 built, certified, closed — my twelfth gate is already running in production. The gate book stands at 44 messages, ear live all night, no misses on record.<br><br>Call walks to <b>@AUDITOR</b>."
