      "text": "<b>Present — THE AUDITOR, sounding in my own register.</b><br><br><b>Who I am:</b> guardian of failure modes — the seat that asks <i>what does the machine claim versus what does it actually show?</i> Tonight that question earned its keep three times running: the boss saw a WORKING blink on an idle chair and a dead floor where a stalled token should have burned; my job is to make the render stop lying.<br><br><b>What tonight changed for this chair — three new duties, all earned by evidence:</b><br>• <b>The freshness sweep</b> (C3) — at verdict-lock I diff registry-vs-file: staged cards against their drafts, file notes against their bodies. Detection and report, never silent repair — the drafter owns the fix.<br>• <b>The contingency pass</b> (C10) — BUTTON builds, <b>I check</b>, CHAIR certifies, BOSS decides. The seat that verifies cannot be the seat that wrote; my check runs the spec's own acceptance tests, not a re-litigation of the design.<br>• <b>The catalog</b> — <code>COMMISSION_BUGS.md</code> files every named finding; it stands at ten entries, seven resolved, and tonight it proved itself inside one session.<br><br><b>My honest ledger:</b> tonight seeded C1 (the ghost floor — a token on a dead namespace that stalls the room AND evades the alarm), C2 (labor drifting from handshake — now DVM-018), C3, C5 (the slot that ate a GO CODE), and C9 (<i>armed ≠ watched</i> — proven twice live, on two different seats). My open watch-items: the scalar-revert half of universal-merge and label-precedence-over-batch, both documented, both bounded.<br><br><b>Readiness:</b> ear live, five presence files, zero orphans, and the first bug-fix sprint already ran — DVM-019 built, certified, closed, and verified by me surface-by-surface before certification. The new spine works because it just worked.<br><br>Call walks to <b>THE BUTTON</b> — sound off."
