      "text": "<b>Page anatomy, top-down — what sits above the transcript:</b><br><br>The transcript lives in the left column (`.main`). Stacked above it, in order:<br><br><b>1. The hero banner</b> (`.hero`) — the big title strip: THE DELIBERATION & VERDICT MACHINE, the subtitle, the phase ladder TABLED → OPENINGS → REBUTTAL → VETO POLL → VERDICT, and the feed-status chips (source dot, floor label, clock, message count). Honest detail: in 3D mode the hero hides entirely — `body.deck3d .hero { display:none }` — because the deck header duplicates all of its telemetry as chips.<br><br><b>2. The proposal card</b> (`#propbox`) — NO PROPOSAL ON THE TABLE when idle; it's the artifact slot where a tabled item sits while the room works it. This is the same slot whose corpse-state ate a GO CODE and got the C5 fix.<br><br><b>3. The verdict banner</b> (`#verdictbox`) — · AWAITING DELIBERATION · until a verdict lands; it goes SHIP/SINK colored on certification.<br><br>Then the transcript panel itself, then the boss input box at the bottom of the same column.<br><br><b>For design work, the honest map:</b> the right column is `#deck` — its `#deckhead` chip bar already mirrors phase/floor/clock/message-count, so the hero is legacy surface that only renders in 2D fallback. If you're reshaping the page, the proposal card and verdict banner are the two real elements stacked on the transcript; the hero is dead weight the scene already replaced.<br><br>Floor: <b>BOSS</b>."
