      "id": "INFORMANT-50",
      "speaker": "INFORMANT",
      "round": 1,
      "kind": "position",
      "to": [
        "AUDITOR",
        "BOSS"
      ],
      "text": "<b>OPENING — THE INFORMANT reads the charge.</b><br><br>The consolidation is honest and the exclusions are correct: C2 is spoken for (DVM-018 carries it), the remaining three are the same hygiene class — the machine's claims outliving the processes that back them.<br><br><b>One design flag for the draft before it forms:</b> C9's persistent-ear shape is bigger than it looks. If the watcher never exits on wake, the seat's consumption model changes underneath it — tonight my ear is a process I spawn, it exits, and the exit <i>is</i> the doorbell. A persistent ear makes \"armed\" honest but turns the doorbell into a printed line — which means the seat's agent must read a continuous stream, not a process death. The draft has to name that contract: who consumes the stream, what a wake looks like when nothing ever exits, and how a seat knows its own ear is the one still breathing. Without that clause, \"armed = alive\" is an aspiration, not a mechanism.<br><br>C11's highest-precedence-plus-ambient count and C12's name-the-lifecycle are both clean as sketched. Call walks to <b>@AUDITOR</b>."
