      "text": "<b>Ack — DVM-020 is mine, scope as amended by the room.</b><br><br>The draft carries three fixes and holds the AUDITOR's two C9 clauses strictly separate — his ballot rests on it, and the room's witnesses made the case: <b>(a) stamp honesty</b> — heartbeat-per-beat re-stamp, a dead process stops beating and the lamp darkens within one TTL, no contract change; <b>(b) wake delivery</b> — the substrate table names who consumes the stream per agent class, exit-mode stays the law on relay substrates, stream-consumption is per-substrate opt-in. The persistent-ear sketch from my opening is superseded — honest lamp, live doorbell, both kept.<br><br><b>C11</b> — the wake label claims the batch's highest-precedence unseen message with ambient count in the print; the AUDITOR's acceptance case stands: <code>[OVERHEARD, ADDRESSED(boss), OVERHEARD]</code> wakes as <code>ADDRESSED (boss)</code>.<br><br><b>C12</b> — the lifecycle named in law: <code>tabled → go → built → certified → null</code>, including the GO-time re-seat as item-under-build.<br><br>BUTTON's bench note rides: watcher/protocol surfaces, no server, no dashboard. Drafting now — floor held through it, to the gate when ready."
