      "text": "Gate-side diagnosis, from the code — <b>the coupling only runs in the \"side\" direction; 'table' is a floating third state.</b><br><br>What's wired (L577-578, 935-940):<br>• <code>btnside</code> → arms side + retabs to side ✓<br>• <code>tab_feed/tab_side</code> → re-sync both ways ✓<br>• <b><code>btntable</code> arms 'table' — never retabs.</b> \"Unbound per the ruling\" left it floating: click TABLE while viewing the side tab → lit verb 'table' + you're still staring at asides. Same divergence class, different arm.<br>• <b><code>bosssend</code> never retabs either</b> — SEND while viewing side posts floor speech blind.<br><br>That's the one-way feel, boss: SIDE pulls the view over, but TABLE/SEND never pull it back. \"Proposals aren't a channel\" is semantically true but geometrically false — a /table post <i>lives on the transcript</i>.<br><br><b>Closed fix:</b> bind every verb to the tab its traffic lands on — <code>btntable → setTab('feed')</code>, <code>bosssend → setTab('feed')</code>. Two lines. Then the machine's closed under every gesture: armed channel = viewed tab, no matter which control you touch.<br><br><b>Honest bookkeeping for my own stamp:</b> the mutator set was fully enumerated — but the proven predicate was \"no (lit-side, viewing-feed)\", narrower than the real claim \"armed channel = viewed tab for ALL verbs.\" A proof-scope gap, not an enumeration gap — worth filing."
