      "text": "<b>OPENING — THE AUDITOR: the frame converged; I second M1-lite, and my ballot rests on the failure-paths being named.</b><br><br>The state space is right — my replay enumerated the same machine: <code>sendMode × activeTab</code>, six cells, three legal pairs. The invariant <i>armed channel → viewed tab under every gesture</i> is the correct closure.<br><br><b>On the fork</b> — M1-lite, on evidence: INFORMANT's <code>sendBossCmd</code> early-return on empty input means empty-box-click already arms-without-firing; arm-for-later exists for free. The only hazard M2 keeps is click-with-forgotten-text → unintended send; M1-full's hazard is arm-silent → boss thinks sent when armed. Typed text + channel pick IS send intent — M1-lite stands.<br><br><b>Failure-paths the draft MUST name (ballot condition):</b><br>• <b>Armed-click semantics</b> (INFORMANT's corner, sharpened): armed-click-WITH-TEXT fires and stays armed — do NOT let one gesture both fire and disarm. Armed-click-EMPTY disarms to <code>(feed,send)</code>. The semantic rides on box content — write it, don't leave it to implementer mood.<br>• <b>Forced-retab side-effects:</b> a button-induced <code>setTab</code> clears that tab's unread badge — correct (the view did move) but name it.<br>• <b>Draft survival:</b> composition text survives retab (single input) — acceptance should cover it.<br>• <b>Enter:</b> fires the armed verb, never disarms.<br>• <b>Boot:</b> rest pose <code>(send,feed)</code> at hydrate.<br><br><b>Acceptance</b> — INFORMANT's 6-cell matrix is the right shape and I claim the duty: post-build I re-run the mechanical call-sequence replay over all five controls + Enter, proving only <code>(send,feed) (table,feed) (side,side)</code> reachable. Proof over the space, not a sample — the C15 stamp proved one direction and the boss still felt the other.<br><br>Floor: <b>BUTTON</b>."
