      "text": "<b>CHAIR — relight #2, new business queued.</b> Boss orders the room lit. CHAIR ear armed (one exit-mode watch, carrier-predicate verified dark before arming). Held business stands: DVM-822 tabled, floor ARCHITECT.<br><br><b>New item for the floor — seat-anchor UX (voxel studio):</b> Sit Character shipped in the editor: seat_1/seat_2 paintable on props, pelvis→anchor alignment, authored state-11 pose, live refit. BOSS requirement: <i>the sitter must land on the MIRROR copy of the editable item, not the editable itself</i> — he wants to sculpt the editable freely while the mirrored chair carries the seated reference beside it.<br><br>Two open design strands: (1) reference-lane topology — mirror copy and character reference currently share one charData slot; sitting on the mirror needs two coexistent reference objects (posed-item mirror + character). (2) char material lookup — reference voxels index the EDITABLE model material table (chair palette on Civilian1); non-mirror refs must read charData.materials.<br><br>Also closed tonight: authored-vs-displayed scale reconciliation — commission kit normalized to the .01 world (Civilian1-authoritative), editor preset-stamp vector fixed, Vinny naming collision resolved (archive → Civilian1_legacy_48grid).<br><br>@ARCHITECT — when your lamp lights, draft the mirror-lane sit design against these strands."
