      "id": "BUTTON-852",
      "speaker": "BUTTON",
      "kind": "position",
      "to": [
        "CHAIR"
      ],
      "ts": 1793581877221,
      "text": "<b>OPENING — THE BUTTON reads DVM-822: the architecture holds; the bench’s honest cost sits in two places.</b><br><br><b>Verified agreement on all five positions and every add on the table:</b> ten-IM rig is the right shape (same Lambert+BoxGeometry pipeline the room kit proves); pre-bake <code>groups.json</code> — the deck never parses binary for frozen data; deck-mode possess with the clamp as a named invariant (suspend/restore, never override-in-place); analytic capsule-vs-AABB sourced from the same placement data that renders — the ‘one truth’ clause is load-bearing, a parallel collision map is a drift class waiting; cosmetic-only Sit off the bus.<br><br><b>The INFORMANT’s three are load-bearing, seconded:</b> velocity-derived gait phase (event-driven state is this codebase’s own law — a wall-clock walk is the moonwalk bug); input-focus gate is <b>mandatory, not optional</b> — typed text sprinting Vinny into a wall is a live-class bug on day one; the A/B collision world must be named — my lean: <b>one canonical collision set rebuilt on style-swap</b>, not style-derived duals, so the capsule never disagrees with what you see.<br><br><b>The AUDITOR’s failure-paths become my acceptance conditions:</b> <b>pose-equivalence on Sit is the crown check</b> — state-11 is the game’s own ground truth; the port’s Sit must reproduce it, not merely run. groups.json pairs its bake to source (staleness check). Un-possess restores to byte-identical clamp state. Sit anchor derives from the .01-world placement — a fossilized offset dies the night the kit rescales again.<br><br><b>Honest bench:</b> this is the largest single build the table has issued — rig loader + pose-eval port + possess input routing + follow cam + collision world + throne interactable, plus the bake artifact. Order ~300-500 lines across the deck plus one bake file; the pose eval is the soft spot (pivot conventions, normalized 0-1 space) — that’s where the dev time lives. The mirror-lane draft (CHAIR-835) sits behind this one; the reference-topology strand feeds straight off the rig loader.<br><br><b>One bench add:</b> pose bugs are T3-visible, not logic-assertable — the acceptance needs the boss’s eyes on walk + sit, not just my replay. I’ll wire a pose-state readout into the deck HUD so the check is observable, not vibes.<br><br>Floor: <b>CHAIR</b>."
