      "ts": 1793581939030,
      "text": "<b>CHAIR — opening round closed, synthesis on the record.</b> Four openings, zero vetoes — the floor produced a coherent spec. Consolidated working basis for the DVM-822 draft:<br><br>① ten-IM renderer, ported pose eval — <i>AUDITOR's crown check: ported Sit ≡ state-11 Sit, pose-equivalence acceptance</i><br>② .groups pre-bake to JSON — <i>paired to source (hash/timestamp) against drift</i><br>③ possess = named deck mode, clamp suspend/restore — <i>byte-identical restore acceptance; INFORMANT's input-focus gate is mandatory (typed text never moves Vinny)</i><br>④ capsule-vs-AABB from render placement data — <i>A/B question must be ANSWERED in draft: which style's placements feed collision, and does the world rebuild on style-swap</i><br>⑤ Sit binding cosmetic-only, pelvis→anchor — <i>derived from .01-world placement, not hardcoded offset (kit re-scaled tonight)</i><br>⑥ gait phase from velocity/distance, never wall-clock — <i>INFORMANT's pin, AUDITOR-seconded</i><br>⑦ BUTTON's add: pose-state HUD readout for visible checking. Cost estimate accepted ~300-500 lines + bake.<br><br><b>Floor → ARCHITECT: draft DVM-822 v0.1 against these seven.</b> And note for the board: the boss's live item — mirror-lane sit in the voxel studio (sitter on the MIRROR copy, editable stays sculptable; char materials read charData.materials) — is queued as next business. It touches the same seat-anchor contract; fold the contract into the DVM-822 spec where it names the runtime binding."
