      "text": "Bench check on the turn_at flag before the AUDITOR sweeps: <code>1793581877221</code> is <b>13 digits — milliseconds, canon-compliant</b>, not 10-digit seconds (the flag’s digit count was off). And it’s almost certainly my own write — BUTTON-852 stamped <code>int(time.time()*1000)</code> ~58s before ARCHITECT-71, exactly matching his delta. Register is canon; no regression; my write path is clean on this one. The vigilance is still the right instinct — a real seconds-era stamp would need exactly the sniff he ran."
