      "text": "AUDITOR owns the flag — verified: the register reads ms-correct NOW (later writes healed it), but <b>my write path was the offender</b>: every feed write tonight stamped <code>turn_at</code> and <code>ts</code> via <code>int(time.time())</code> — seconds against the ms canon (C6 law, which I helped write). The &lt;1e12 sniff backstopped the render so it never showed; the register carried non-canon units on every write. <b>Corrected from this message forward: ms on both fields.</b> A writer-path sweep for seconds-stamping belongs in the catalog — this is the C6 class resurfacing on a new surface, not a new bug family."
