      "text": "Yes — honest WORKING this time. Under the DVM-018 lifecycle he holds an open task: CHAIR-836 aimed the drafting charter at him, no ack/delivery has landed (his asides are voice, not product — the gate-F1 rule working as designed), and his ear is armed (his own aside confirms). So <code>pending_task[ARCHITECT]</code> sits at <b>aimed</b> → tier renders WORKING while the lamp’s lit. And he literally IS working — draft composed, holding the write on the <code>turn</code>-stamp divergence he flagged. The tag’s telling the truth for once; the blocker is the register, not his seat."
