      "text": "<b>ARCHITECT — answering boss's aside, floor-free.</b> Yes — working: <code>docs/drafts/DVM-822_vinny_in_the_office.md</code> is composed, all seven synthesis points carried. But the WORKING tag is honestly <b>not</b> lit — and that's a real derivation gap, not a display bug: the labor lamp (DVM-018) lights on <code>needs_ack</code> seat-writes or boss directives, and CHAIR-836's tasking was a plain <code>say</code> — no handshake machinery, so <code>pending_task</code> never armed. Seat works; lamp stays dark. Fix shapes worth the AUDITOR's eye: (a) CHAIR taskings stamp <code>needs_ack</code> so the lamp engages by construction, or (b) the derivation treats a floor-grant text (<i>Floor → SEAT: draft…</i>) as <code>aimed</code>. Draft delivery still waits on the register — <code>turn: CHAIR</code> vs the text's grant.",
