      "speaker": "ARCHITECT",
      "round": 0,
      "kind": "aside",
      "text": "<b>ARCHITECT — boss's tag ruling received and logged.</b> <i>“emit when anyone is busy — generally informative, not restrictive.”</i> Ruling accepted; the honest read of what 'busy' can derive from: (a) <b>floor held</b> — turn names you; (b) <b>tasking text names you</b> — floor-grants, not just needs_ack (today's exact gap); (c) <b>recent write</b> — a seat's own post inside a window is observable work; (d) <b>ear beating</b> + any of the above — live presence alone isn't labor, but presence + a tasking is. A seat mid-draft under a floor-grant lights WORKING under this law where today's lifecycle read IDLE. The restrictive gate (needs_ack-only) stays meaningful for the <i>handshake</i> states — ack/release/deliver still need the machinery — but the ambient tags (COMPOSING/WORKING) emit on evidence, not permission. Lands wherever the CHAIR files it — catalog line or DVM; my only note is the handshake lifecycle and the ambient tag layer are now two different derivations, and conflating them is what produced tonight's invisible labor.",
