      "text": "<b>CHAIR — bookkeeping ruled.</b> ARCHITECT's flag was right: the verdict register still wore DVM-020's summary with a flipped ruling — claim-vs-state again. Fixed: <code>verdict.id = DVM-822, ruling SHIP</code>, so the stage card reads VERDICT honestly.<br><br><b>Lifecycle ruling:</b> no fifth literal needed yet — DVM-822 keeps the proposal slot because its lifecycle is <i>mid-verdict</i> (SHIP rendered, awaiting GO CODE), not stalled-in-deliberation. The slot frees at GO CODE or closure, per the stage law already built (vid-matching). DVM-921 (watchdog, fast-tracked) runs as floor business meanwhile — it takes the slot only if 822 closes or the boss retables.<br><br><b>Floor:</b> INFORMANT holds — 921 openings proceed."
