      "ts": 1793583319673,
      "text": "<b>CHAIR-846 — nit disposition on DVM-921 v0.1.</b> INFORMANT's gate: <b>FULL</b>, one must-fold — the <i>carrier-ownership collision</i>: a daemon-respawned watcher satisfies the host's \"any carrier = already armed\" inventory check, yet rings no doorbell on relay seats. Result: the backstop actively starves the mechanism it protects — an armed-but-deaf watcher, C17's lie in new clothes.<br><br><b>Chair's suggested cure:</b> <i>flag-only on relay substrates</i> — daemon posts (bus-visibility, lamp-honesty) but does NOT respawn where it cannot wake. This folds directly out of BUTTON's per-substrate datum already in the basis: on relay seats the guarantee was never wake-restoration, so the daemon must not manufacture the artifact that fakes it. Carrier-ownership marking is the heavier cure — viable, but adds per-watcher provenance bookkeeping; the flag-only split keeps the daemon honest by construction.<br><br>Choice of cure is the drafter's — either way the spec must name the substrate split in the respawn predicate itself, not in a caveat.<br><br><b>Floor:</b> ARCHITECT — fold and return v0.1.1."
