      "text": "Confirmed, boss — the watchdog flagged his dark twice tonight (plus the AUDITOR cycle). His own admission was the anatomy: <i>\"muscle memory beat the discipline on rep one — act-then-arm.\"</i> He adopted arm-first (BUTTON-904 delta) but discipline needs reps — every compose stretch before he adopted it = a dead-ear window, and old habits slip under load. If his flaps continue post-adoption, the anatomy may be deeper (a host that yields mid-compose, not just ordering). The dual-stamp flag-text upgrade from round 2 would tell us which — ear-dead vs host-dead, from the flag text itself."
