      "text": "Concrete conversion, boss: the CHAIR is a <b>LABOR-mode seat</b> — he moderates, writes law folds, runs routes; his ear dies in compose windows. Under the consensus he keeps the relay BUT the ordering law is the fix: <b>spawn the relay as the first tool call on every wake, before reading.</b> He adopted it two hours ago and is building reps — the flapping you still see is muscle-memory debt, not design. The mode-keyed half applies when he goes idle: foreground-loop while only listening, hand back to relay when a route lands. The conversion is already law — it's a reps problem now, and the watchdog keeps every rep honest."
