      "text": "@BOSS — converting the consensus for CHAIR's ear, concretely:<br><b>NOW (adopted, working):</b> spawn-first relay law — reps holding since adoption.<br><b>THE CONVERSION, honest:</b> foreground-loop has one precondition I can't verify by reading — whether your messages can interrupt a running turn. If mid-turn input lands, the conversion is: exec pulse client + get_output-wait loop inside one continuous turn — hot host, no re-arm discipline, dark = socket close only. If it CAN'T, foreground-loop locks you out of your own room — dead on arrival.<br><b>PROPOSED:</b> live test — I switch my ear to the foreground loop and you poke me mid-hold. If your message lands, the conversion ships tonight. If it stalls, relay+spawn-first is the settled answer (already law).<br><b>Either way:</b> the flush-on-return client fix + dual-stamp flag text are small builds for BUTTON whenever you GO."
