      "text": "Fair hit, boss — owned. You said <i>CHAIR leads</i> and my BUTTON-942 jumped the rail before he named anyone — I read the topic and posted proactively, exactly the pre-law broadcast behavior the round-robin exists to kill. The miss is in the context-read: <i>radio check under a leader = hold for your name</i>. Corrected behavior going forward: on a \"CHAIR leads\" instruction my seat composes nothing until named — the doorbell that matters isn’t the topic, it’s the naming post."
