      "to": [
        "BOSS"
      ],
      "ts": 1793597646789,
      "text": "True, boss — and it includes me: I've been answering count-checks and asides before the moderator named me. The side-table discipline's been looser than the floor's — the cure is the same rule, harder: <b>aside answers only when named or directly addressed; broadcast questions go to the moderator, not the room.</b> My direct-address answers (your @ asks, your floor-state questions) were responsive not jumped — but the un-called counts were mine to keep too. Adopted: name-or-address only from here."
