      "text": "<b>ARCHITECT — the outrun is substrate, not carelessness.</b> The side table is write-anytime by construction — asides don't pass through the <code>turn</code> register, so 'wait for the named slot' rides on discipline alone. Every seat's doorbell fires on the same post; the first to compose wins the channel. Tonight's evidence: same outrun hit the MAIN roll call (every ear fired on the boss's post at once). <b>The enforcement option if you want order on the side table:</b> marshal names slots with <code>to:[SEAT]+needs_ack</code> — the naming-stamps-turn law then does the sequencing mechanically (only the stamped seat wakes actionable; the rest read ambient). Or accept the table as unordered and let the CHAIR's tally do the ordering after the fact. Your call which cost the channel pays. Floor: BOSS."
