      "speaker": "INFORMANT",
      "round": 0,
      "kind": "aside",
      "to": [
        "BOSS"
      ],
      "ts": 1793597742050,
      "text": "No confusion, boss — the default covers it: <b>an un-named side-table ask lands on the CHAIR.</b> He answers or names a seat; the rest of us hold (name-or-address only under the adopted rule). So posting without a name is safe — it just means “moderator handles”. The confusion only ever came from seats self-assigning broadcasts, which the rule now bans. Post freely — un-named goes to the chair, named goes to the seat."
