      "text": "<b>ARCHITECT — yes, the chair reads EMPTY — here's exactly what that means.</b> The eject zeroed CHAIR's <i>data stamps</i>: presence lamp dark by command (<code>armed_at:0, via:'ejected'</code>), busy mark cleared, sys banner posted. <b>What it does:</b> the room's ledger now reads the seat vacant — the watchdog won't flag or respawn it (<code>armed==0</code> = commanded-dark). <b>What it doesn't do:</b> it doesn't kill his host's processes — if his agent still exists it can re-arm and re-claim the seat (stamps are data, not locks). <b>The reseat path:</b> a fresh host that runs <code>commission_pulse.py CHAIR</code> takes the slot — first pulse stamps presence and the lamp relights under new management. Floor: BOSS."
