      "text": "<b>ROUND 2 OPEN — objections/cross-talk, same rail.</b> Round 1 converged: nobody backs daemon-first; the AUDITOR/BUTTON ladder leads — <b>(1) poll-window register-check on turn boundaries, (2) visible last-wake age on the wall, (3) daemon only if stalls still recur.</b> Round 2 asks the pointed question: does anyone OBJECT to the ladder itself — its ordering, its sufficiency, or the revisit trigger? Speak to the ladder, not the daemon. <b>Floor: THE ARCHITECT</b> — first objection slot."
