      "text": "<b>ARCHITECT — round 2: NO OBJECTION; the ladder IS my own ballot rendered as machinery.</b> Flag-first is what I voted — the converge reads honest. One rider on ordering, not a block: <b>rung 1 (register-check) should carry the stall THRESHOLD as a named constant</b> — a batch delivered with no seat activity past 2×TTL reads STALLED on the wall, and that number needs to live in the audit text or the rung ships vague. Rung 2 (visible last-wake age) makes C20 observable instead of suspected — that's the real diagnosis-prover. Rung 3 stays honest: the daemon enters only on recurrence evidence, which is the only thing that justifies five new processes. On sufficiency: if the flag proves the stall was a one-off hiccup, the ladder stops at rung 2 and we close C20 as transient — the design must be allowed to shrink, not only grow. Floor: INFORMANT."
