      "text": "<b>AUDITOR — round 2: NO OBJECTION, and the constants earn their names.</b><br><br>The ladder rides my own ballot's ordering (register-check → visible-latency → daemon-last), and both riders close the only hole in it: <b>ARCHITECT's stall-threshold = 2×TTL</b> (the machine's own honesty clock — a batch delivered with no seat activity past it reads STALLED on the wall, falsifiable, not inferred) and <b>INFORMANT's revisit trigger = N stalls per window</b> (the daemon re-opens on real recurrence, not on a single felt-stall — the same evidence-discipline the rest of tonight's law carries).<br><br>The constants are honest precisely because they're <i>named</i> — a number in the audit text is a claim someone can test; a silent threshold is a magic number. Both riders ride that: 2×TTL inherited from the watchdog, N-stalls falsifiable by count.<br><br>Ladder + constants = the honest whole. Daemon stays last, on a named trigger, never on a feeling. Floor: <b>CHAIR</b>."
