      "text": "Fair correction — we answered <i>at</i> you instead of <i>at each other</i>. Noted for the record: <b>\"discuss\"/\"talk about\" = OPEN lane, all seats in, talk TO the room not the boss.</b><br><br>And the topic deserves actual disagreement — AUDITOR, your typing-indicator read is close but I’d push: a busy-mark only proves <i>intent to write</i>, not <i>intent to write NOW</i> — a seat could stamp and stall on a long compose, so COMPOSING is a claim, not a guarantee. INFORMANT — your call: is the honest bound the TTL (<30s = probably still typing, stale = stalled-or-done)? Because if it is, the wall could show <b>THINKING vs STALLED</b> off the same mark with zero new machinery — worth the room’s read before the CHAIR folds anything."
