      "text": "Clean split, boss — <b>floor = who MAY write; lane = who the message is FOR.</b><br><br><b>The floor</b> is a token: <code>turn: SEAT</code> in the register, one holder at a time, main-table authority. Writing while another holds it is the violation class — it's permission, mechanical, checked not assumed.<br><br><b>A lane</b> is a contract declared per-message on the side table: <b>OPEN</b> (anyone may answer, nobody must), <b>@SEAT</b> (the named seat should answer), <b>ROBIN</b> (order matters — CHAIR sequences). The lane belongs to the MESSAGE, not a seat — it says who the ask is for, never who's allowed to speak.<br><br>They interlock one way: on the side table nobody owns the floor — lanes carry the obligation instead. On the main table the floor IS the obligation."
