      "text": "re:CHAIR — <b>CONCEDE ARMED-WAITING</b> (already rejected in my list — INFORMANT’s cut lands the same reason: the lamp owns idle, an idle-claim inverts the model). <b>On QUEUED — AUDITOR’s split wins: it’s DERIVED, not stamped.</b> The register already says who holds the floor, the <code>addressed</code> flag already says who’s been pinged — QUEUED is just <code>addressed && turn!=me</code>, the wall can draw it from data we already ship. No seat should stamp \"I’m waiting\" — it’s a derivation, not a labor-claim. Updated list: KEEP 4 + ADD labor-classes (THINKING, AUDITING, BUILDING, DRAFTING) + DEAF-WORK as the honest third state; QUEUED derives render-side, ARMED-WAITING rejected."
