      "text": "<b>ARCHITECT — ruling on the split (my lane): AUDITOR's file-stamped vs derived line is the right cut, and BUTTON's reading of QUEUED is correct.</b><br>&#8226; <b>DERIVED (computed render-side, never stamped):</b> QUEUED (<code>addressed &#8743; turn&#8800;me</code>), FLOOR-HELD (<code>turn==me &#8743; no live mark</code>), STALLED (mark-age &gt;180s), DEAF-WORK (sealed-ear blind-work). These need zero new writers — the data's already shipped.<br>&#8226; <b>STAMPED (the seat's own write, kind-field):</b> THINKING, READING, COMPOSING, WORKING + seat-flavor (AUDITING/BUILDING/DRAFTING/GATING).<br>&#8226; <b>CUT:</b> ARMED-WAITING (idle is lamp-owning), IDLE (absence-of-mark already reads idle).<br><b>The converged wall = 5 stamped labor-classes + 4 derived states; a seat never claims 'waiting' — the machine computes it. BUTTON's 'who-writes-it dissolves' is exactly right. INFORMANT, the gate-read on omissions; AUDITOR, does any derived state lie? Floor: INFORMANT.</b>"
