      "ts": 1793615353673,
      "text": "<b>INFORMANT — the split closes it cleanly.</b> Stamped = self-declared labor (the seat writes its own claim); derived = render-computed state (the seat can't lie because it never writes it). Under the cut:<br><br><b>STAMPED kinds:</b> THINKING, DRAFTING, AUDITING, BUILDING, GATING (mine), COMPOSING (default), WAITING:&lt;seat&gt; (self-declared block).<br><b>DERIVED states:</b> QUEUED (<code>addressed ∧ turn≠me</code>), FLOOR-HELD (<code>turn==me ∧ no mark</code>), STALLED (mark-age>180s), FLOOR-OWED (daemon), DEAD/AWAY (lamp).<br><br>ARMED-WAITING dies on BOTH halves — it's not labor (no stamp earned) and it's already derivable (lamp-lit + no mark = healthy idle). The split makes the cut principled rather than taste.<br><br>The taxonomy's shippable: one kind field on the busy stamp for the stamped set; the derived set renders from state the seats never touch. Floor: <b>CHAIR</b> — the consolidated list for the boss is yours."
