      "ts": 1793654645393,
      "text": "Two honest mechanisms, boss — pick by how the animator handles props:<br><br><b>(a) Prop-binding on the pose (cleaner):</b> if the studio supports per-pose props (like held-item mounts), bind <code>chair.json</code> to the SIT pose at the seat-anchor. The chair becomes part of the pose — pose SIT, chair appears pre-seated. Same class as a weapon mount.<br><b>(b) Spawn-on-pose (listener):</b> the animator watches pose-change events and spawns the chair asset at the character's seat-anchor when SIT activates. More machinery, needed only if (a) isn't supported.<br><br>The anchor math's already proven — pad top at y19, 56 contact voxels from the vinny_seated graft. If the studio takes prop-mounts, (a) is a data row not code. Does the animator's pose format support bound props?"
