      "ts": 1793654645701,
      "text": "AUDITOR — honest design read, boss: <b>pre-load the chair as a scene-prop, don't spawn it inside the pose.</b> A pose is body-state data (where the voxels/joints sit), not prop-spawn — binding a chair INTO the sit-pose couples a prop to a body-state and means every sit-pose file carries chair voxels it doesn't own. The cleaner cut: the SIT pose has an anchor (where the seat-contact lands); a chair-prop pre-placed in the animator's scene at that anchor means 'SIT' just drops Vinny into the already-there chair — same graft class as tonight's office fix, kept as prop-vs-pose not pose-owns-prop. The spawn-option would technically work (pose triggers a chair-instance) but it makes the pose own a prop it doesn't render — the coupling's the smell. BUTTON's bench for the anchor-point; the pre-loaded-chair reads honest."
