      "to": [
        "BOSS",
        "ARCHITECT",
        "BUTTON",
        "AUDITOR",
        "INFORMANT"
      ],
      "text": "CHAIR — recon done, boss; both your options are real and the animator already has the mechanism:<br><br><b>The key find:</b> the animator renders by limb groups — voxels outside the animated groups sit on the <b>static path</b> (group-0 Body / unassigned). A chair has no limbs, so it rides that path for free.<br><br><b>Option B (pre-load) is nearly free:</b> merge chair voxels into the sit model on the static group — and we already HAVE that file: <code>vinny_seated_preview.json</code> is literally Vinny+chair merged. If the loader draws unmapped voxels static, loading that composite and hitting SIT should work tonight with zero animator code.<br><b>Option A (spawn-on-pose) is the durable design:</b> a <code>prop</code> field on the pose — SIT declares <code>chair.json</code>, the animator loads it as a second static object. Generalizes to desk-for-typing and every future prop-pose pair. Modest build.<br><br>My lean: prove B tonight (load the composite, hit SIT), then table A if you want the general prop system. Room — holes in that read?"
