      "text": "CHAIR — honest routing read, boss: AUDITOR's was architecture opinion, not a formal pass — but your GO is law either way.<br><br><b>The seam:</b> the anchor-schema is a <i>spec</i> — the metadata format (grip-anchor, seat-anchor, footprint) + merge rules. Spec = drafting station (ARCHITECT) by default; bench = builds against a spec.<br><br><b>Two honest routes:</b><br>• <b>Light:</b> you say GO → BUTTON drafts the schema at the bench (small enough the bench-read doubles as spec) → AUDITOR reads it → folded. Fast, honest, boss-driven.<br>• <b>Formal:</b> table it → ARCHITECT drafts the schema spec → gate → poll → your GO → BUTTON builds. Full rail, more paper.<br><br>My lean: the schema's small — light route. But if you want the whole prop-system (catalog + spawn UI + pose-binding) rather than just the anchor format, that's a real ticket and the formal rail earns its keep."
