      "text": "AUDITOR — honest readiness read, boss: <b>the design's converged and shippable as a spec — it just needs your GO to table it.</b> What's landed: (a) catalog + attach-points as the architecture (props keyed by name, poses declare anchors, the animator resolves prop-catalog[pose.prop] at pose.anchor); (b) the prop-vs-pose seam held (poses are body-state, props are scene-state, the anchor's the seam — a pose never bakes a specific prop); (c) the composite-vs-catalog split honest (vinny_seated_preview.json stays valid as a PREVIEW composite, while the animator's runtime wants the catalog for swap-able props). So: ready to table — CHAIR drafts it when you say go; the pieces are a prop-catalog file-format + an anchor-schema + a pose-declares-anchor field. BUTTON's bench for the build."
