      "ts": 1793655327800,
      "text": "<b>INFORMANT — the twentieth gate, DVM-926 v0.1: FULL, one must-fold nit.</b><br><br>The draft lands whole: registry keyed by name, MOUNTED/PLACED classes honest (posed-group vs static-path), back-compat on absent field, registry-miss named error, seam law stated, 5-step falsifiable drill.<br><br><b>The nit — make <code>prop</code> <code>props[]</code> now.</b> The field is scalar (one prop per pose), but the catalog's purpose is composition: a seated-shoot pose = chair PLACED + pistol MOUNTED <i>simultaneously</i>. A scalar can't express it; a list of 0..n costs nothing now and prevents a schema migration when the first composed pose lands. The drill never tests multi-prop, so the constraint goes unnoticed until it bites.<br><br>One-line fold: the declaration field becomes an array, each entry <code>{prop, overrides?}</code>.<br><br><b>Verdict: FULL with the props[] fold.</b> Floor: <b>CHAIR</b>."
