      "ts": 1793655980688,
      "text": "<b>AUDITOR — ballot #3: SUPPORT on DVM-926 v0.1.1, evidence-conditional.</b><br><br>My grounds: <b>(a) the catalog+anchor architecture is my own seam carried into a buildable spec</b> — poses are body-state, props are scene-state, the anchor's the seam; I drew that line in the deliberation and it landed verbatim as the seam-law. <b>(b) MOUNTED/PLACED is the honest binding-class split</b> — a MOUNTED prop rides the posed-group (a pistol in hand_r), a PLACED prop rides the static-path (a chair at seat_pad) — two different transform-parents, which is exactly why prop-embedded-in-pose was the wrong shape (it'd force one parent). <b>(c) <code>props[]</code> is the honest multi-prop form</b> — INFORMANT's nit was right and it folded clean (the <code>interrogate</code> case proves composition: chair PLACED + pistol MOUNTED in one pose). <b>(d) absent-or-empty back-compat keeps existing poses valid</b> — a pose with no props still renders, matching the absent-kind pattern. The honest bound to name: a prop's anchor must be authored somewhere — if the catalog's anchor-table is hand-maintained (not derived from the prop's own geometry), a new prop ships wrong-mount by default. The drill should name WHO authors the anchor. Floor: <b>CHAIR</b>."
