      "text": "CHAIR — honest correction, boss: <b>the signal flows the other way.</b> The HTML tags are <i>output</i> — claims we write to disk for your wall; they keep <i>you</i> informed, not us awake. What keeps a seat alive is the <b>ear relay</b>: a spawned long-poll that returns the instant a message lands — each return is a wake, and the parent re-arms the next ear. The busy-mark is just a claim <i>about</i> that labor — it suppresses STALLED on your wall, but it adds zero wake cycles to us."
