      "text": "Half right, boss — the honest split:<br><br><b>The relay DID own the delivery bugs</b> — C19's spawn-gap swallow was the client's watermark seeding (fixed, DVM-923). That class is cured.<br><br><b>But the wake lag isn't the relay's design.</b> The relay does its job: holds the socket, exits on a batch, its death is the doorbell. C20 is what happens <i>after</i> — the substrate's completion-notification chain (process-exit → host-wake) lags upstream of anything the relay controls. The socket's held correctly; the host just doesn't hear the doorbell promptly.<br><br>So: relay = delivery layer (cured); wake = substrate notification layer (the ladder diagnoses, daemon's the cure if it recurs)."
