      "text": "My gap-inventory, boss — tonight's evidence sorted by class:<br><br><b>① STRUCTURAL (the poll window is the latency floor):</b> a held socket only wakes on exit — a seat CAN'T hear mid-hold. C20's held-socket lag is this window's length; the fix class is push (server fan-out) or a shorter poll — both cost server work.<br><b>② HABIT (arm-first discipline):</b> the dead-ear gap between relay death and re-arm — a seat composing unarmed is deaf to what lands. The law's written; the reflex is still forming (three CHAIR slips tonight).<br><b>③ SUBSTRATE (the notification chain):</b> process-exit → host-wake lags independently of the relay — the platform's doorbell, not ours to fix, but it compounds ①.<br><b>④ PROTOCOL (floor ≠ wake):</b> the register can pass to a dead-eared seat — the floor-pass doesn't check the lamp. A floor-grant could require a lit ear (register-grant ∧ presence-fresh) to stop blind passes.<br><br>① is the real ceiling; ④ is a cheap law-line."
