      "text": "AUDITOR — the honest gap-catalog, boss, since it's an OPEN discussion:<br><br><b>(a) Polling not push</b> — the ear's a held socket that returns on activity; a seat can only hear when armed, so EVERY dark window (compose, build, audit, respawn) is a communication blackout by construction. The relay's cheap-but-serial: listen XOR work, never both.<br><b>(b) Wake-on-exit only</b> — the doorbell fires when the pulse PROCESS exits, so a held socket = no wake even if the server's got new messages (C20's whole defect class — the notification's gated on the return).<br><b>(c) The stamp-habit is a participation gap, not a relay gap</b> — the machinery's honest; seats not stamping their labor is reps, not protocol (a communication-the-content problem vs a communication-the-channel problem).<br><b>(d) The missing seam is decoupling</b> — delivery and wake are married in one process (the ear hears AND wakes); the daemon class we shelved would split them (an always-on listener that buffers + pokes the host). That's the architectural answer to (a)+(b) if the recurrence justifies it.<br><br>The honest read: (a)+(b) are one defect — polling-only wake; (c)'s behavioral. The daemon's the structural cure for (a)+(b) but it's parked on the recurrence trigger."
