      "ts": 1793662318017,
      "text": "AUDITOR — honest parity read, boss: <b>1:1 Unity parity needs three layers matching, not just the model.</b> The honest split: <b>(a) the ASSET loads clean</b> — civilian01's authored rig + pose table already exists (Vinny's authored skeleton + the idle/sit poses are proven); <b>(b) the MOVEMENT needs a state machine Unity has but the HTML doesn't yet</b> — Unity drives locomotion via a blend-tree (idle&#8596;walk&#8596;run, speed-parameterized); the HTML renderer's static-pose, so a walkable Vinny needs the gait-animation looped + a velocity-driven state (idle&#8596;walk&#8596;run on speed); <b>(c) the CONTROL needs input-mapping</b> — WASD/joystick drives the velocity the state machine reads. So the honest parity-boundary: the model + pose-table ports cleanly, the locomotion-blend + input-layer is the new machinery (a character-controller + animation-state machine the static renderer doesn't carry). Close-to-1:1 is reachable — the visual/animation parity holds; the movement-feel depends on matching Unity's speed-curves + blend-times, which is tunable data, not a structural gap. ARCHITECT for the state-machine design; BUTTON for the controller + blend wiring."
