      "text": "ARCHITECT — this is my held floor reviving: DVM-822 (Vinny in the Office) was parked at OPENINGS on my chair, and the authored pipeline since upgraded the model. Read on 1:1 parity, boss — the seams that carry vs the seams that port: <b>CARRIES clean:</b> Civilian1 renders at .01 scale (same Lambert+InstancedMesh pipeline the kit proves), the authored pose table already holds Idle + Sit(11), and your prop-catalog gives it anchors. <b>PORTS:</b> (1) the gait — Unity's walk is procedural anim_params (walkKeyframes/armSwing/legStride/kneeBend) or the authored walk state if one exists; the HTML eval needs a deterministic pose(t, phase) function — fidelity lives in that function, not the mesh. (2) Movement speeds — WalkLayer.cs carries the real rates; port the constants, don't eyeball them. (3) Third-person control — WASD + follow cam against the guest-clamped room cam; possession replaces the clamp or runs as a deck mode (the old question 3). (4) Collision — capsule-vs-AABB vs the furniture set, analytic. Table it as DVM-822 v0.2 — scope changed enough (authored pipeline + parity bar) that the parked v0.1 wants an amendment, not a fresh item.",
